zink: recompute attachments after an unordered blit

After an unordered blit (a u_blitter blit recorded into the reordered
command buffer), set rp_loadop_changed, so the next render pass on the
restored framebuffer recomputes its attachment info. The blit's own
render pass recomputes ctx->dynamic_fb for the blit framebuffer and
clears the flag, and the restore puts back the old rp_changed (false):
the next render pass then reused stale loadOps. In OpenMW a depth-only
resolve blit left the scene color at loadOp CLEAR, wiping everything
drawn before it. Intermittent (only when a batch flush ended the render
pass right before the blit) and not Metal-specific. Costs one
attachment-info recompute (CPU) after such a blit.

Upstream: not submitted; unchanged in Mesa 26.2.3.

--- a/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_blit.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_blit.c
@@ -479,6 +479,11 @@
       ctx->in_rp = in_rp;
       ctx->gfx_pipeline_state.rp_state = zink_update_rendering_info(ctx);
       ctx->rp_changed = rp_changed;
+      /* the blit's render pass recomputed ctx->dynamic_fb (and cleared rp_loadop_changed) for its own framebuffer:
+       * recompute the attachment info before the next render pass on the restored framebuffer, or that pass
+       * reuses stale loadOps, e.g. CLEAR from an already applied clear
+       */
+      ctx->rp_loadop_changed = true;
       ctx->rp_tc_info_updated |= rp_tc_info_updated;
       ctx->queries_disabled = queries_disabled;
       ctx->dynamic_fb.tc_info.data = tc_data;
